Subject: [PATCH] audio: Mac ARM compressor math from the profile

Under a macOS ARM profile, DynamicsCompressorNode converts between
decibels and linear gain with log10 and exp10 routines that round the
way the Mac ARM math library does. The host's math library rounds these
slightly differently, and the difference shows up in the compressor's
output samples, which a page can hash. x86 hosts with AVX and FMA run
the same arithmetic with hardware fused multiply-add. Other profiles
keep the default math.

